om has only increased  demand for these services an estimated  700 000 skilled trades people are  expected to leave the workforce and  retire within the next seven years  according to the latest research from  rbc and that means even more of these  workers are going to be needed in these  fields  michelle crisp left her job as a  personal trainer three years ago to  found her own contracting company she  says being handy runs in the family my  dad is like a  true renaissance man he's kind of a jack  of all trades he could do everything  from fix a car it's a plumbing  electrical framing drywall during covid  she's quadrupled her staff hiring all  women doing her part in an industry that  hasn't always been welcoming to women  the patriarchy is pretty deep in this  world  misogyny and everything else a lot of  the people that reach out to me are are  females i find that they feel a lot more  comfortable with having a female  contractor in their home  she hopes her pandemic pivot encourages  other women to get outside their comfort  zone and try something that really pays  off  ann gaviola global news toronto  toronto makes noise for a wild card  showdown next the blue jays push to the  playoff  the toronto blue jays have returned home  to twice the stadium noise ontario's  government has allowed rogers center to  double the seating capacity it's now  capped at 75 percent which is about 30  000 people everyone must be fully  vaccinated and it's just in time for a  make or break series opener the blue  jays are in a three-way race to win one  coveted spot and as erik sorensen  reports young talent may be the team's  ticket to the top  this team is a joy to watch not just a  power hitting playoff contender they're  so cheerful doing it the home run jacket  just one feature of a club that is young  and talented led by 22 year old  superstar vladimir guerrero jr yeah they  have fun with it there's a lot of energy  with this team and that comes naturally  from being young 